			"title": "The height of Oyo",
			"text": "Oyo rules a metropolitan core and the Egbado corridor to the sea, where Ajase (Porto-Novo) ships enslaved people to European traders. Dahomey has paid tribute since 1730. The Egba and Igbomina towns are tributaries. Oyo settled colonists along the Egbado corridor, at Ilaro and Imeko, to hold the road to Badagry and Porto-Novo; Sabe and Ketu in the west, and at times the Borgu and Nupe borderlands, paid tribute. Oyo's cavalry has defeated Dahomey in 1728 and forced it to pay yearly tribute; it took eleven invasions before Dahomey was fully subjected in 1748.",
